('1b725fd5-ea19-464d-acd6-b85ee56e1a19', 'Every Friday afternoon, Mr. Chen takes his class of young students to the school garden. Each child has their own small plot of soil to take care of. Some children grow flowers, while others plant vegetables like carrots and beans. Mr. Chen teaches the students how to water the plants gently and remove weeds without hurting the roots. The students also learn to check the soil to see if the plants need more water. At the end of the school year, the class holds a small garden party where families come to see what the children have grown. Many parents say the garden project is their children''s favorite part of school.', 1, -2.0, true);
